James inquired about the entropy of a single fair coin toss. I explained that entropy measures uncertainty in outcomes and can be calculated using the entropy formula \( H(X) = - \sum_{i} p(x_i) \log_b p(x_i) \). For a fair coin, with equal probabilities \( p(H) = 0.5 \) and \( p(T) = 0.5 \), the calculation revealed that the entropy is 1 bit. This indicates that a single fair coin toss conveys 1 bit of information.
